WEBVTT

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:05.672
In our city, there are many things.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.307
Large buildings.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.441
Parks.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.576
Hospitals.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.478
Shopping malls.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.946
We have cars.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.948
We also have a monorail.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:15.982
And TVs,

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.117
and telephones,

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:20.153
and even machines with which
to listen to music.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:24.691
I live in the apartment building
Ms. Miranda owns

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.023
in the unit Mr. Roy lives in.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:39.294
I love this town.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:01.261
Good morning.
This is your morning news.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.363
It turned out well,
if I do say so myself.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:07.867
Oh, my, it says the RUC announced
yet another new product.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.869
Just how much money
do they plan to make?!

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.927
Hey!

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.041
Why are you here?

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:19.779
Oh, please! I told you, remember?
That I'd be living here?

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.514
I don't recall giving you my permission!

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.784
See, our hideout got raided by the police,

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.519
and I got separated from my bros,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.221
so I ran for all I was worth.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.689
Listen to me!

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.525
Miss Rose...

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:35.462
That must have been awful.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.729
Yeah, it was, really.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.698
Listen to me when I'm talking!

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:42.335
Hey, I'm supposed to have
the best of luck today.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.437
What about you, Solty?

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:48.965
I do not know when I was born, so...

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:54.347
Hey, people born in November
are supposed to have the worst luck!

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.542
Mister, when were you born?

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.778
This is the worst...

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:10.196
You know the continuation of the fairy tale
I've wanted to hear about?

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:16.658
If it's eternal happiness,
I'll forge it with my own hand

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:28.348
It's like we were both seeking
a coincidence that was off by a page

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.517
And that's how fate
brought us together

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:38.691
More than those words
that you once kept to yourself

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:47.600
It's the kindness that made you
keep them to yourself

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:54.607
That I want to have faith in now

00:02:54.607 --> 00:03:02.248
You know, we'll be living alongside
uncertainty from now on

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:08.655
We used to have nothing to lose,
but that's not us now

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:16.362
You know the continuation of the fairy tale
I didn't know about before?

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:22.602
If it's eternal happiness,
I'll forge it with my own hand

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:26.436
It's something to build up
bit by bit

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.047
Continuing with today's news...

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.782
But this sure is a dirty place.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.517
"The Imp's Visit"
But this sure is a dirty place.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.586
"The Imp's Visit"
Do you actually do any cleaning?

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.678
"The Imp's Visit"
It's none of your business!

00:03:44.421 --> 00:03:46.056
What is the matter?

00:03:46.056 --> 00:03:48.592
As long as I'm going to be living here,

00:03:48.592 --> 00:03:51.891
you guys are going to maintain
a certain level of cleanliness.

00:03:55.899 --> 00:04:00.336
An unclean environment is
also bad for your skin, you know.

00:04:02.706 --> 00:04:04.901
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:04:06.743 --> 00:04:08.412
Where's the dresser?

00:04:08.412 --> 00:04:10.380
The shower works, right?

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.083
The shampoo has to be a TTC blend.

00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:14.151
Same with the body soap.

00:04:14.151 --> 00:04:15.319
Hey!

00:04:15.319 --> 00:04:18.455
Cleaning gets done every day.
Same with laundry.

00:04:18.455 --> 00:04:23.527
However, do not wash my things
together with that old man's things.

00:04:23.527 --> 00:04:24.328
Hey...

00:04:24.328 --> 00:04:27.331
In the morning, make vitamins
and minerals a priority.

00:04:27.331 --> 00:04:30.100
No oily or high-calorie items.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.303
The only tea to be served is rosemary.

00:04:33.303 --> 00:04:35.271
After all, my name is Rose.

00:04:36.974 --> 00:04:38.909
Come on, take a dig at me.

00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:40.110
What?

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.181
And no coffee. The water
you use cannot be tap water.

00:04:44.181 --> 00:04:47.517
Buy Clear Water and use that. Got it?

00:04:47.517 --> 00:04:48.785
I see...

00:04:48.785 --> 00:04:50.787
That's enough already!

00:04:50.787 --> 00:04:54.391
It's not like I've given
you permission to live here!

00:04:54.391 --> 00:04:57.194
Sheesh, you're not the type to let
yourself get swept along, are you?

00:04:57.194 --> 00:04:59.263
Like hell I'm going to get swept along!

00:04:59.263 --> 00:05:02.499
Then let's decide by a majority vote.

00:05:02.499 --> 00:05:06.236
Who's in favor of me living here?

00:05:06.236 --> 00:05:09.139
Me!

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:11.164
Me...

00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:18.849
M-Me...

00:05:18.849 --> 00:05:22.886
I mean, it seems like she cannot
go home, so I feel bad for her.

00:05:22.886 --> 00:05:25.188
Besides, if Miss Rose
comes to live with us,

00:05:25.188 --> 00:05:27.257
I think it would surely be fun.

00:05:27.257 --> 00:05:29.259
You made a great point just now!

00:05:29.259 --> 00:05:31.193
Don't be ridiculous!

00:05:33.897 --> 00:05:35.198
Mr. Roy, where to?

00:05:35.198 --> 00:05:36.665
Work.

00:05:38.535 --> 00:05:41.638
Get out of here before I come back!

00:05:41.638 --> 00:05:43.407
Got it?!

00:05:43.407 --> 00:05:45.307
Got it?!

00:05:50.814 --> 00:05:52.482
Is he getting enough calcium?

00:05:52.482 --> 00:05:54.780
Yes, probably.

00:06:00.924 --> 00:06:02.459
They have got to be kidding me!

00:06:02.459 --> 00:06:05.155
I'm not going to put up with having
another noisy one around!

00:06:14.638 --> 00:06:16.840
I-I'm sorry!

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.332
I'm sorry! I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.277
This is the worst...

00:06:33.223 --> 00:06:36.593
I heard she's set herself up
at your place...

00:06:36.593 --> 00:06:38.929
That thief, Rose.

00:06:38.929 --> 00:06:40.564
How do you know about that?

00:06:40.564 --> 00:06:43.467
She came by yesterday to
let us know she was moving in.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:45.059
With sweets.

00:06:46.269 --> 00:06:49.406
She's conscientious
about some odd things.

00:06:49.406 --> 00:06:51.675
Would you like some?

00:06:51.675 --> 00:06:53.310
But you know...

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.612
...isn't this kind of bad?

00:06:55.612 --> 00:06:59.983
You're technically a hunter
and having a thief living with you is...

00:06:59.983 --> 00:07:02.352
It's not as if I've given my permission.

00:07:02.352 --> 00:07:04.254
Oh, it's no problem.

00:07:04.254 --> 00:07:06.289
Even if a thief is living with a hunter,

00:07:06.289 --> 00:07:10.193
all we have to say is that
he was hired to do just that.

00:07:10.193 --> 00:07:11.595
More importantly,

00:07:11.595 --> 00:07:15.499
is it true that the police
raided their hideout?

00:07:15.499 --> 00:07:17.167
Yes, it's true.

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:19.302
There's a log of it on the net, too.

00:07:19.302 --> 00:07:21.204
What about the whereabouts
of the older two?

00:07:21.204 --> 00:07:24.775
It looks like the police
don't know yet, either.

00:07:24.775 --> 00:07:28.472
The official word is that
they're currently searching for them.

00:07:59.376 --> 00:08:01.037
Sheesh!

00:08:10.353 --> 00:08:12.981
Oh, welcome back.

00:08:16.426 --> 00:08:19.029
Oh, right there!

00:08:19.029 --> 00:08:21.497
Keep working on that spot!

00:08:28.505 --> 00:08:32.709
M-My stuff...

00:08:32.709 --> 00:08:35.679
We're done renovating the room.

00:08:35.679 --> 00:08:37.704
Thanks for your hard work!

00:08:43.253 --> 00:08:45.288
My room...

00:08:45.288 --> 00:08:46.823
- Ow, that hurt...
- Excuse me!

00:08:46.823 --> 00:08:49.626
We've brought the closet
and sideboard!

00:08:49.626 --> 00:08:52.062
I have a cash-on-delivery package
here for a Ms. Rose!

00:08:52.062 --> 00:08:53.196
Dinner delivery service!

00:08:53.196 --> 00:08:56.399
Is this the right place for the
dress and makeup delivery?

00:08:56.399 --> 00:09:00.403
Yes, yes! Please bring
all of it over here!

00:09:00.403 --> 00:09:03.073
Oh, I made that room mine.

00:09:03.073 --> 00:09:06.009
Privacy and stuff is important, you know?

00:09:06.009 --> 00:09:07.010
Y-You...

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:08.578
Here.

00:09:08.578 --> 00:09:11.047
It's important to you, right?

00:09:11.047 --> 00:09:13.884
Since this was the one thing
that was kept clean...

00:09:13.884 --> 00:09:16.553
Excuse me, the payment for the package...

00:09:16.553 --> 00:09:19.623
That will be 78,000 traz.

00:09:19.623 --> 00:09:21.458
Yes, yes!

00:09:21.458 --> 00:09:25.758
Um, it must be cramped,
what with another person here now.

00:09:28.532 --> 00:09:31.763
If you'd like, you could come to my place...

00:09:34.838 --> 00:09:37.739
I-It's rather noisy...

00:09:40.577 --> 00:09:43.079
- Thank you very much!
- Thank you very much!
- Thank you very much!

00:09:43.079 --> 00:09:44.748
What's the meaning of this?!

00:09:44.748 --> 00:09:48.818
There's nothing to explain. I just
made things more comfortable for me.

00:09:48.818 --> 00:09:49.920
Put things back the way they were.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:50.754
What?!

00:09:50.754 --> 00:09:52.889
That room is my room!

00:09:52.889 --> 00:09:54.457
Then, what about my room?

00:09:54.457 --> 00:09:55.759
Sleep on the floor or something.

00:09:55.759 --> 00:09:59.095
What?! That's not fair!

00:09:59.095 --> 00:10:02.656
Then... Okay! I have an idea!

00:10:08.772 --> 00:10:10.763
How about a match?

00:10:28.058 --> 00:10:32.290
And put on some clothes
before you clean up the room.

00:10:34.998 --> 00:10:36.863
I swear...

00:10:42.172 --> 00:10:44.470
It's important to you, right?

00:10:50.547 --> 00:10:52.415
Oh!

00:10:52.415 --> 00:10:55.748
I should've made the bet,
so she'd have to leave!

00:10:57.587 --> 00:11:02.025
Staying one step ahead of the enemy
is the way thieves operate.

00:11:02.025 --> 00:11:06.363
But two people in this room
is way too cramped.

00:11:06.363 --> 00:11:09.232
My stuff won't fit in here.

00:11:09.232 --> 00:11:12.068
Is that so?

00:11:12.068 --> 00:11:13.503
Are these yours?

00:11:13.503 --> 00:11:17.474
Oh, no. Those belong to Miss Rita.

00:11:17.474 --> 00:11:19.976
She is Mr. Roy's daughter.

00:11:19.976 --> 00:11:22.706
Though, she is currently missing.

00:11:25.282 --> 00:11:30.553
Um, if it is too cramped,
would you like me to leave this room?

00:11:30.553 --> 00:11:34.353
I could just as easily sleep on the sofa.

00:11:35.358 --> 00:11:38.895
There's no need for that.

00:11:38.895 --> 00:11:42.599
After all, one of my objectives
in coming here...

00:11:42.599 --> 00:11:44.863
...is you.

00:12:08.858 --> 00:12:10.660
Doctor...

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:14.964
There's a limit to the treatments
we can offer at this facility.

00:12:14.964 --> 00:12:18.802
Unless we obtain antibodies,
further treatment is...

00:12:18.802 --> 00:12:20.603
Oh, it's Big Brother!

00:12:20.603 --> 00:12:22.205
Big Brother Andy!

00:12:22.205 --> 00:12:23.740
Quiet, now.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:27.477
Come on, don't make a racket.
We're in a hospital.

00:12:27.477 --> 00:12:29.279
Larry...

00:12:29.279 --> 00:12:31.181
Yeah, I know.

00:12:31.181 --> 00:12:34.742
Don't worry. We'll get
the antibodies real soon.

00:12:35.952 --> 00:12:38.355
When you get resemblized,

00:12:38.355 --> 00:12:45.195
there's always some degree of rejection
where the mechanical parts meet the body.

00:12:45.195 --> 00:12:48.221
And it's the antibodies
that suppress that reaction.

00:12:50.033 --> 00:12:52.268
For people who have residency,

00:12:52.268 --> 00:12:56.339
antibodies are as easy
to obtain as cold medicine,

00:12:56.339 --> 00:12:59.740
but for unregistered residents,
it's not so easy.

00:13:00.977 --> 00:13:03.580
That's why I steal.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.782
- So that's where...
- Oh, that is a no.

00:13:05.782 --> 00:13:09.753
- What?
- I will not assist you in stealing.

00:13:09.753 --> 00:13:12.455
Because Mr. Roy will get mad at me.

00:13:12.455 --> 00:13:16.893
O-Oh, please, did I say anything
about helping me steal?

00:13:16.893 --> 00:13:22.165
U-Um, I have a different favor
to ask of you, Solty.

00:13:22.165 --> 00:13:24.656
A different favor?

00:13:47.123 --> 00:13:50.927
That's it for work today.

00:13:50.927 --> 00:13:53.963
Is that a special shipment
of resemble antibodies?

00:13:53.963 --> 00:13:55.799
Yes, that's right.

00:13:55.799 --> 00:13:58.601
They've been attacked by thieves
a couple times in the past, right?

00:13:58.601 --> 00:14:00.103
Will they be all right?

00:14:00.103 --> 00:14:02.338
It's not our job.

00:14:02.338 --> 00:14:05.942
Besides, I hear they're
assigning escorts starting today.

00:14:05.942 --> 00:14:09.145
Defensive heavy machinery, EV-002.

00:14:09.145 --> 00:14:13.016
They're apparently looking
to hire civilian hunters, too.

00:14:13.016 --> 00:14:15.348
Civilian hunters, huh?

00:14:19.756 --> 00:14:23.326
I saw an intriguing job from the RUC.

00:14:23.326 --> 00:14:24.360
What is it?

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:28.298
The job is to escort a shipment
of resemble antibodies.

00:14:28.298 --> 00:14:30.934
They've been attacked by thieves
a couple times in the past,

00:14:30.934 --> 00:14:33.970
so it's probably
a countermeasure against that.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.573
What do you want to do?
Will you take it?

00:14:36.573 --> 00:14:40.243
No, it's not my problem.

00:14:40.243 --> 00:14:41.444
You're not taking it?

00:14:41.444 --> 00:14:42.579
No.

00:14:42.579 --> 00:14:45.315
But it does bother you, right?

00:14:45.315 --> 00:14:48.944
When you hear about thieves
at a time like this...

00:15:23.319 --> 00:15:28.222
Now, all that remains is
to watch the results unfold.

00:16:02.325 --> 00:16:05.762
I just want you to run a little.

00:16:05.762 --> 00:16:07.196
You want me to run?

00:16:07.196 --> 00:16:11.534
Right. Down that big street.

00:16:11.534 --> 00:16:13.436
Down that street?

00:16:13.436 --> 00:16:14.270
That's right.

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:16.739
How far?

00:16:16.739 --> 00:16:18.730
As far as you can go.

00:16:20.376 --> 00:16:22.745
Why am I doing this?

00:16:22.745 --> 00:16:26.282
I want to measure your physical abilities.

00:16:26.282 --> 00:16:29.252
Or are you not even allowed to just run?

00:16:29.252 --> 00:16:30.687
No, that is not...

00:16:30.687 --> 00:16:32.455
Then it's settled.

00:16:32.455 --> 00:16:35.391
Start running when this clock
counts down to zero.

00:16:35.391 --> 00:16:37.293
O-Okay.

00:16:37.293 --> 00:16:40.421
Run as fast as you can
with all your might, okay?

00:16:45.868 --> 00:16:48.166
It is almost time.

00:17:00.416 --> 00:17:02.680
Just a little longer.

00:17:08.691 --> 00:17:11.127
What? What are you doing here?

00:17:11.127 --> 00:17:14.330
Are you planning on hitting
the resemble antibody truck?

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:17.700
Did you come to interfere
in our operation?!

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.702
It's not my problem.

00:17:19.702 --> 00:17:22.438
Since I didn't take the job.

00:17:22.438 --> 00:17:24.407
You guys do what you want.

00:17:24.407 --> 00:17:28.277
Then what is it?
I'm busy right now.

00:17:28.277 --> 00:17:29.979
Don't drag Solty into this.

00:17:29.979 --> 00:17:31.503
Huh?

00:17:33.149 --> 00:17:35.618
Are you that worried about Solty?

00:17:35.618 --> 00:17:38.154
Well, of course you'd be.
You're her father, after all.

00:17:38.154 --> 00:17:40.423
If that's what you want to think, fine.

00:17:40.423 --> 00:17:43.126
But you don't have to worry.

00:17:43.126 --> 00:17:45.995
We'll be the ones who do
the actual dirty work.

00:17:45.995 --> 00:17:48.691
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:18:10.119 --> 00:18:12.451
Hey, are you listening to me?!

00:18:13.856 --> 00:18:15.118
It's time.

00:18:16.325 --> 00:18:17.724
Go!

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.295
Solty!

00:18:31.474 --> 00:18:33.910
Solty!

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:36.470
Oh, Mr. Roy...

00:18:46.656 --> 00:18:50.456
Wh-What was that? Did they
take one down already?

00:18:52.161 --> 00:18:54.530
It's showtime!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.829
Ow, that hurt.
I crashed into someone...

00:18:59.302 --> 00:19:00.599
Oh?

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.910
Taking on two of them
would've been rough, even for us.

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.502
One to go!

00:19:12.315 --> 00:19:14.340
Anti-laser coating?!

00:19:20.423 --> 00:19:21.858
They're pretty good.

00:19:21.858 --> 00:19:24.588
Then how about this?!

00:19:28.931 --> 00:19:30.626
Fire!

00:19:33.369 --> 00:19:34.961
Damn it!

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:42.478
Wh-What the hell?! This isn't any
different from all the other times!

00:19:42.478 --> 00:19:43.968
Exactly!

00:19:49.485 --> 00:19:52.477
I'll kindly ask you to pull over
without a fight.

00:20:03.366 --> 00:20:05.768
Come on, everyone's waiting.

00:20:05.768 --> 00:20:07.904
Let's hurry up and take these back.

00:20:07.904 --> 00:20:08.371
Yeah.

00:20:08.371 --> 00:20:10.373
Yeah.

00:20:10.373 --> 00:20:12.041
Miss Rose!

00:20:12.041 --> 00:20:14.143
Miss Rose!

00:20:14.143 --> 00:20:16.379
I-I...

00:20:16.379 --> 00:20:18.848
...crashed into someone just now.

00:20:18.848 --> 00:20:21.751
Don't worry.
That was totally okay.

00:20:21.751 --> 00:20:25.488
It's exactly what I expected of you.

00:20:25.488 --> 00:20:26.856
I see...

00:20:26.856 --> 00:20:28.289
Solty!

00:20:29.292 --> 00:20:30.993
Mr. Roy...

00:20:30.993 --> 00:20:32.094
You idiot!

00:20:32.094 --> 00:20:33.863
Hey, Mister! Solty didn't really...

00:20:33.863 --> 00:20:34.897
You, too!

00:20:34.897 --> 00:20:37.127
I told you not to drag her into this!

00:20:39.669 --> 00:20:41.804
I'm sorry.

00:20:41.804 --> 00:20:42.738
We're going home.

00:20:42.738 --> 00:20:45.274
Oh, b-but...

00:20:45.274 --> 00:20:47.071
We are going home!

00:20:56.986 --> 00:20:58.977
What was up with that?

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:05.761
Did you hear?

00:21:05.761 --> 00:21:08.865
They ended up losing that shipment
we saw yesterday anyway.

00:21:08.865 --> 00:21:10.199
Huh.

00:21:10.199 --> 00:21:13.803
But more importantly,
I heard the road's a mess now.

00:21:13.803 --> 00:21:15.464
The road?

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.780
Like I keep telling you,
don't make a racket.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:26.749
Thank you. You've been a great help.

00:21:26.749 --> 00:21:28.951
This should last us for a while.

00:21:28.951 --> 00:21:30.720
Oh, we just did what we always do.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:33.055
Do you have a minute, Brother?

00:21:33.055 --> 00:21:36.684
I just had another great idea.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:58.311
On a clear day in the park

00:21:58.311 --> 00:22:01.247
Looking up at the sky

00:22:01.247 --> 00:22:09.814
There was a tiny little cloud
that almost vanished

00:22:12.492 --> 00:22:17.263
Letting the wind
take us where it will

00:22:17.263 --> 00:22:20.200
We live freely

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:28.241
We make our way,
walking a little at a time

00:22:28.241 --> 00:22:33.013
We're the same

00:22:33.013 --> 00:22:37.784
This precious time

00:22:37.784 --> 00:22:41.621
Each time we meet

00:22:41.621 --> 00:22:51.164
This feeling of not being alone
turns into kindness

00:22:51.164 --> 00:22:57.504
I can turn it into the courage
to believe in someone

00:22:57.504 --> 00:23:09.939
And surely, before I vanish
into the far reaches of that sky...

00:23:16.489 --> 00:23:20.226
Miss Rose, I will not become a thief.

00:23:20.226 --> 00:23:22.996
What?! Come on, why not?!

00:23:22.996 --> 00:23:24.731
Next time, "Revenge".

00:23:24.731 --> 00:23:26.665
Go back home already!
